<Project>

  <!--
    Solution-wide MSBuild properties. Picked up automatically by every
    project under this directory.

    NOTE on build output paths: this file previously redirected all build
    output to .artifacts/ at the repo root via <ArtifactsPath> to dodge
    Windows' 260-char MAX_PATH limit (the Microsoft.PowerShell.SDK package
    fans out deeply-nested runtime folders that overflow when combined with
    our src/<project>/bin/<configuration>/... layout).

    The ArtifactsPath approach turned out to be incompatible with the
    Windows Application Packaging Project (.wapproj) used by
    SharedMailbox.Package — the wapproj's restore/publish targets assume
    conventional in-project obj/ paths and silently fail to generate
    wappublish/<rid>/project.assets.json under the redirected layout,
    breaking MSIX publish.

    Resolution: long-path support is enabled at the OS level via:
        Set-ItemProperty `
          -Path "HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\FileSystem" `
          -Name LongPathsEnabled -Value 1 -Type DWord
    This is a one-time per-machine setting documented in docs/Setup.md.
    With long paths enabled, conventional in-project obj/bin layouts
    work fine and the wapproj is happy.

    If a future contributor reintroduces ArtifactsPath, expect MSIX
    publish to fail with "wappublish/win-x64/project.assets.json not found".
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- intentionally empty; see comment above -->
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
